  {
   "k": "1345498",
   "en": "The below is ⟦0⟧ player suggested strategies for ⟦1⟧. Bear in mind, due to the dynamic nature of the game, it may unfold differently for other players.",
   "frags": 2
  },
  {
   "k": "hovn2f",
   "en": "Playing as ⟦0⟧ is very hard, the first problem that needs to be addressed is the player's almost total lack of industry. ⟦1⟧ actually holds the title for having the lowest starting industry out of any nation in the game (not counting any releasable nations). To which it shares it with ⟦2⟧, ⟦3⟧ and ⟦4⟧.",
   "frags": 5
  },
  {
   "k": "ip4qjz",
   "en": "Mengjiang"
  },
  {
   "k": "1ht2myx",
   "en": "Gansu Ma"
  },
  {
   "k": "hzman0",
   "en": "Khotan Ma"
  },
  {
   "k": "rd4rdj",
   "en": "Pick \"Develop Jinan\" as the first focus. Immediately rush it down until you get everything necessary to produce and build anything. Your goal will be to declare and unite all of the Chinese nations one by one, even sooner depending if Japan decides to go with its fascist branch or not. Take \"Secure Internal Politics\" and go for opposition, in order to go down and produce and get more manpower out of it. Pick a few decisions to improve on Han Fuju's traits, as having the title as 'Unreliable Opportunist' isn't a fitting title to lead the entirety of China."
  },
  {
   "k": "2xct48",
   "en": "If the player wants to do the other part, make sure you prepare yourself to fight China and the rest of the warlord nations, the player only has to worry about Japan keeping its word to have you in their faction, in order to go as far as unite all of China. Fighting the Chinese can be relatively tedious. Shanxi and Hebei Chahar being relatively easy to take down with the outmaneuvering strategy. And China would be a difficulty as they have more territory, strength in numbers and factories. If the player has finally taken China with the Japanese help, make sure that they do the most of effort to leave little to no lands to give to Japan. Finally with the Chinese United Front being dealt with, by using the same outmanoeuvring and pin down attack strategies, Shandong Clique can take any side and core between Communist, Nationalist Chinese focuses. With this done and if the player has completed all of the warlord focuses of Shandong Clique, it is time to rush and go for Warlord subjugation in the generic Nationalist China focus tree. It would give a few wargoals for the player to strike and annex the warlords. Alternatively, go with the \"Invite Foreign Investors\" by rushing down all the way until you reach the \"One China Policy\"."
  },
  {
   "k": "13amqt5",
   "en": "Considering that the \"Renegotiate the Unequal Treaties\" focus is usually bypassed as Shandong Clique doesnt have the national spirit. If the Ma Cliques and the rest of the West sided warlords aren't yet at war with Japan, it is a good opportunity to pick targets one by one. Be vary of the territories. Of the said nations. The Northeastern Army, in comparison to Sichuan and Communist China, is an easier target. Whereas the other two tend to increase their army, and utilize their mountainous terrain. In alternative to that, use the border conflict decision missions as an alternative to gain territory against the neighbors. Make sure to fix the supply routes, research trains and improve on division templates. Otherwise, if that proves to be obsolete, simply declare war on them by \"One China Policy\" focus, battle them in a preferable terrain. Or, research mountaineer divisions to fare better in the mountainous battlefields."
  },
  {
   "k": "1jxku5z",
   "en": "In addition, Shandong Clique can ironically become the second most industrial power in China, only behind Chiang's Flag of China China, thanks due to both its Warlord and Chinese shared focus trees."
  },
